# Resource monitoring

Disk thresholds were introduced:

```bash
DISK_WARNING=80
DISK_CRITICAL=90
```

Logic:

```text
< 80%       PASS
80–89%      WARNING
>= 90%      CRITICAL
```

Memory monitoring followed the same model:

```bash
MEMORY_WARNING=80
MEMORY_CRITICAL=90
```

A controlled disk-warning test was performed by lowering the threshold rather than dangerously filling the filesystem.

The resulting state was:

```text
WARN: Root filesystem utilization is 10%

Warnings Detected: 1
Failures Detected: 0
Overall Status: WARNING
```

with:

```text
exit code = 2
```

The corresponding WARNING email was successfully received.

