# Development and deployment workflow

During the lesson we discovered that editing `/usr/local/bin` directly through VS Code Remote SSH produced:

```text
EACCES: permission denied
```

This led to a better deployment model.

The editable source lives under the Git repository:

```text
engineering-notes/
└── 01-linux/
    └── Management-scripts/
        └── fleet-healthcheck.sh
```

The production copy lives at:

```text
/usr/local/bin/fleet-healthcheck.sh
```

Workflow:

```text
VS Code
   ↓
Management-scripts/
   ↓
Edit
   ↓
bash -n
   ↓
Git
   ↓
sudo install
   ↓
/usr/local/bin/
```

Deployment:

```bash
sudo install -m 755 \
fleet-healthcheck.sh \
/usr/local/bin/fleet-healthcheck.sh
```

Integrity can be verified:

```bash
sha256sum fleet-healthcheck.sh
sha256sum /usr/local/bin/fleet-healthcheck.sh
```

Matching hashes prove that the deployed artifact matches the source.

