# Command Reference

| Command / Construct | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `systemctl is-active SERVICE` | Check service state |
| `systemctl is-active --quiet SERVICE` | Machine-friendly service-state check |
| `systemctl stop SERVICE` | Stop service |
| `systemctl start SERVICE` | Start service |
| `systemctl status SERVICE` | Inspect service |
| `systemctl list-units --type=service` | List systemd services |
| `journalctl -u SERVICE` | Inspect service journal |
| `ss -ltn` | Display listening TCP sockets |
| `ss -ltnp` | Include owning process |
| `ss -ltn "sport = :80"` | Match TCP port 80 exactly |
| `lsof -i :80` | Find processes using port 80 |
| `ps -fp PID` | Detailed process information |
| `ps -p PID -o args=` | Display process command line |
| `df -P /` | Filesystem utilization in predictable format |
| `free` / `free -h` | Memory statistics |
| `apt list --upgradeable` | Show pending package upgrades |
| `grep -q` | Quiet pattern matching via exit status |
| `awk` | Extract/process structured text |
| `$1` | First positional function/script argument |
| `((COUNT++))` | Increment Bash numeric variable |
| `$'\n'` | Bash newline character |
| `printf "%s"` | Controlled string output |
| `bash -n SCRIPT` | Validate Bash syntax without execution |
| `echo $?` | Inspect previous command's exit code |
| `sha256sum FILE` | Calculate file integrity hash |
| `install -m 755` | Deploy a file with specified permissions |
| `exit 0` | Successful/healthy execution |
| `exit 1` | Critical/failure execution |
| `exit 2` | Warning execution |
